<title>USA: Hawaiian Electric Q3 shr falls to $0.57.</title>
<headline>Hawaiian Electric Q3 shr falls to $0.57.</headline>
<dateline>HONOLULU 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996	  Q3	   1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.57		    $0.86</p>
<p> Net			 17,872		   25,151</p>
<p> Revs		     284,417		  261,886</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  30,465		   29,881</p>
<p>					 9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.91		    $2.13</p>
<p> Net			 57,604		   61,878</p>
<p> Revs		     738,918		  797,241</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  29,058		   30,178</p>
<p>					 12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.44		    $2.86</p>
<p> Net			 73,219		   82,797</p>
<p> Revs		   1,047,050		  982,251</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  30,025		   28,917</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name Hawaiian Electric Industries Inc.</p>
<p>Q3, 9 mos and 12 mos 1996 include charges for special one-time assessments by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) on deposits insured by the Savings Association Insurance Fund. ASB's assessment was estimated to be $8.3 million after-tax and was accrued in September 1996.</p>
<p>Excluding the charge, Q3, 9 mos and 12 mos 1996 net income would have been $25.7, $65.9 and $81.6 million, respectively. Earnings per share would have been $0.84, $2.18 and $2.72, respectively.</p>
</text>
